from pathlib import Path
import json
w=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;root=w.parents[2];target=root/'rust-star/reports/32k-baseline-cbb078bb'
def read(p):return json.loads(p.read_text())
a=read(w/'independent-audit.json');assert a['passed'];c=read(w/'results/paired-summary.json')['contexts'][0];profile=read(w/'profile32k.json')
s=(w/'report-outline.md').read_text();marker='## Results and next milestone';s=s[:s.index(marker)]
s+='## Results\n\nFive valid first-attempt pairs; no invalid attempts. Values below are median ± median absolute deviation (MAD), not confidence intervals.\n\n'
s+='| Metric | Rust Star | Oracle-v4 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n'
for label,key,scale,unit in [('Steady decode','gen_steady_tps',1,'tokens/s'),('All 128 decode steps','gen_tps',1,'tokens/s'),('First decode step','gen_first_ms',1,'ms'),('Prefill','prefill_ms',.001,'s'),('Whole process','process_wall_ms',.001,'s')]:
 s+='| '+label+' | '+' | '.join(f"{c[role][key]['median']*scale:.3f} ± {c[role][key]['mad']*scale:.3f} {unit}" for role in ['candidate','oracle'])+' |\n'
s+='| Peak process memory | '+' | '.join(f"{a['memory_distributions'][role]['median']:.3f} ± {a['memory_distributions'][role]['mad']:.3f} GiB" for role in ['candidate','oracle'])+' |\n'
r=c['candidate_over_oracle']['gen_steady_tps'];slow=c['candidate']['prefill_ms']['median']/c['oracle']['prefill_ms']['median']
s+=f"\nThe median paired steady-decode ratio is **{r['median']:.5f}×** Rust/reference, with MAD {r['mad']:.5f} and range {r['min']:.5f}–{r['max']:.5f}. The approximately {(r['median']-1)*100:.2f}% median difference is small and the pairwise range crosses parity. These five runs do not establish a robust decode speed advantage.\n\nPrefill is **{slow:.2f}× slower** by the ratio of latency medians. Rust also uses about {a['memory_distributions']['candidate']['median']-a['memory_distributions']['oracle']['median']:.2f} GiB more peak process memory. The first-decode-step metric excludes prefill; it is not end-to-end time to first output. Process wall time includes initialization and other overhead outside the internal timers.\n"
s+='\n## Separate profile\n\nThe profile matches the fixed transcript and is excluded from paired throughput. Its eight decode stage shares use Metal timestamp counters scaled to completed layer GPU intervals. Encoder splitting perturbs execution; these figures guide investigation rather than measuring uninstrumented throughput.\n\n| Decode stage | GPU ms / steady token | Share of transformer GPU interval |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n'
for stage in sorted(profile['stage_profile']['stages'],key=lambda x:x['steady_share'],reverse=True):s+=f"| {stage['name']} | {stage['steady_gpu_ms_per_token']:.3f} | {100*stage['steady_share']:.2f}% |\n"
s+='\nAt 32K this mode does not collect per-layer or per-kernel prefill attribution. The uninstrumented paired candidate runs do expose these aggregate medians:\n\n| Prefill interval | Median seconds |\n| --- | ---: |\n'
for label,key in [('Transformer setup','prefill_transformer_setup_ms'),('Transformer execution wall','prefill_transformer_wall_ms'),('Transformer GPU','prefill_transformer_gpu_ms'),('Tile GPU','prefill_tile_gpu_ms'),('Total reported host overhead','prefill_host_overhead_ms')]:s+=f"| {label} | {a['prefill_timing_medians'][key]/1000:.3f} |\n"
s+='\nThese intervals overlap or nest and their independent medians must not be summed into an exact partition. GPU execution is the largest measured component; setup is also material. The measurements do not identify a particular slow prefill kernel.\n'
s+='\n## Next milestone\n\nClose the 32K prefill gap: first add explicitly ineligible per-chunk/per-stage profiling across all 43 layers, accounting separately for setup, encoding/waits, and GPU work. Use it to select and implement the largest measured C0-safe improvement, preserving full-logit checks and shorter controls, then repeat this five-pair protocol. Reusing prefill resources may reduce the measured setup cost, but its payoff is a hypothesis until measured. Broader native contexts and the 256K primary result remain future work.\n'
s+=f"\n## Audit and limits\n\nThe independent audit rehashes all twelve warmup/timed measurement bundles, checks both frozen executable hashes, verifies candidate transcripts, recomputes all summary distributions and paired ratios, regenerates the official summary byte-for-byte, and checks profile scope and stage shares. It records {a['host_observations']} host observations and {len(a['unusual_thermal_observations'])} unusual thermal observations. Background applications and load observations remain in the evidence. Five pairs describe this fixed workload on this host; they do not establish general model quality or broad speed superiority.\n\nThe summary's `headline_eligible` flag means schema/protocol eligibility only. This is a 32K development baseline, not the charter's 256K headline.\n"
(target/'README.md').write_text(s)
print(target/'README.md')
